          "The relational view agrees that discernment is needed. A method is not good just because it works; it must also be honest, respectful of persons and not manipulative. But the answer to bad techniques is good ones, used wisely, not rejecting medicine and therapy as such. And there is no either/or between praying and treatment: Hezekiah received both a promise and a poultice. Prayer and medicine are two ways of receiving from the same Father."
